    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0a13490_3abdaccf",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/mqtt/mqttconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 38827
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T09:36:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Potential bug with client_id in multi-scheduler deployments:\n\nIf client_id is specified in the connection config, all scheduler instances initialize their MQTT client using that exact same ID.\n\nWhen a client connects with an ID already in use, the broker must terminate the existing connection. In a multi-scheduler deployment, this causes the schedulers to enter an infinite disconnect/reconnect loop fighting each other for the connection.\n\nSuggestion: If client_id is provided in the configuration, append a unique scheduler component identifier (or a random suffix) so each scheduler instance has a distinct client ID on the broker",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "1f5a0017723349a0ac89ff073f9794343c663487",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
